Atlas overlay patch 0005: privacy/metrics-default-off
Why: usage statistics are off by construction. The metrics reporting pref was registered with
the value of the stats-consent file in the user data directory; it is now registered false, so
no file, import or leftover state can turn it on. The managed policy MetricsReportingEnabled
(shipped by the WolOS system package) still governs it, and crash upload still reads that policy.
Not in patches-0 (it lists the policy, A7); added because a policy file is absent on a plain
install of the package outside WolOS.
Files: chrome/browser/browser_process_impl.cc
Test filter: *MetricsReporting*; chrome://local-state shows user_experience_metrics.reporting_enabled false
Rebase risk: L (one line; two inherited patches edit other parts of this file)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunk in a file the inherited series patches)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, prepared tree with the inherited and platform series applied

--- a/chrome/browser/browser_process_impl.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/browser_process_impl.cc
@@ -1368,7 +1368,7 @@
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
 
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(metrics::prefs::kMetricsReportingEnabled,
-                                GoogleUpdateSettings::GetCollectStatsConsent());
+                                false);
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(prefs::kDevToolsRemoteDebuggingAllowed, true);
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(prefs::kDevToolsRemoteDebuggingEnabled, false);
 
